Well, you may just have to stay unsatisfied. Formal
probability and statistics mixes incredibly poorly
with gut intuition about how things "should work".

Here, this might help.

Suppose that your first five games are:

NYYYY

For whether N = spellbookful
            Y = spellbookless

Does it take a test of five more games to get five
"Y" games in a row?

No, it is possible to do that in just _one_ more
game. That's where your intuition is failing you
about how the odds should be calculated.

